Common Amiga socket headers for the pre-1.0 IPv6 ABI correction
============================================================

Baseline: AmigaPorts/amiga-netinclude
Commit: c9fed00ba3186d9b02bc0de13eb0cf3c83f087e1
https://github.com/AmigaPorts/amiga-netinclude/pull/2

Only netinet/in.h and sys/socket.h are carried here. They retain the
upstream license notices and Latin-1 encoding; trailing spaces are removed.
The baseline includes codewiz's self-contained-header fixes; no generated
library vectors change.

Changes relative to that baseline:

  netinet/in.h: define SIN6_LEN and insert sin6_len before sin6_family.
  sys/socket.h: define the 128-byte BSD sockaddr_storage with ss_len and
                ss_family, naturally aligned for sockaddr_in/in6 on m68k.

The library, applications and staged Developer drawer use these same files.
Put Developer/include before the compiler's NDK/netinclude directory. The
remaining common headers come from that directory; no compiler cache is
modified. This overlay can be replaced by an upstream pin when accepted.

The old pre-release IPv6 structure put its family byte at offset zero.
All provided IPv6 applications must be rebuilt with the corrected headers
and shipped with bsdsocket.library ABI 4.11 or later from AmiNetXDuo.
Existing IPv4 layouts, function vectors and option numbers are unchanged.

Run the compile/layout gate with:
  python3 tests/toolchain/check_ipv6_sdk.py --toolchain /path/to/toolchain

Runtime coverage is in tests/ipv6/ipv6_socket_test.c and its run-socket.sh
harness. Changes to the header ABI require updating both sides together.
